# MAYOR OF TUAL

# MALUKU PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF TUAL CITY

# NUMBER 03 OF 2019

# CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

# BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

# MAYOR OF TUAL,

Considering:  
a. that as citizens, women and children have the right to obtain protection from any act of violence committed against them that causes physical or psychological harm, as part of the recognition and enforcement of human rights;  
b. that protection for women and children victims of violence is an effort to provide a sense of security and freedom from all acts of violence guaranteed by Pancasila as the state philosophy, the Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia as the highest legal basis in the state as well as various other laws and regulations;  
c. that protection of women and children victims of violence is one aspect of the duties and responsibilities of regional government in providing protection and services to the community;  
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of Tual City concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;  

In View of:  
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;  

2. Law Number 60 of 1958 concerning Stipulation of Law Number 23 of 1957 concerning Establishment of Level II Autonomous Regions Within the Level I Autonomous Region of Maluku (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1958 Number 111, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1645);  
3. Law Number 6 of 1974 concerning Basic Provisions on Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1974 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3039);  
4. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);  
5. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention On The Elimination Of All Forms Of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 19, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3668);  
6. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Minimum Age For Admission To Employment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);  
7. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);  
8. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4928);  
9. Law Number 31 of 2007 concerning Establishment of Tual City in Maluku Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 97, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3209);  
10. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4389);  
11. Law Number 17 of 2014 concerning People's Consultative Assembly, House of Representatives, Regional Representative Council and Regional House of Representatives (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 182, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5568);  
12. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended by Law Number 2 of 2015 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 24, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5657), and Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);  
13. Government Regulation Number 58 of 2005 concerning Regional Financial Management (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 140, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4578);  
14. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);  
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines and Development for Establishment of Integrated Service Centers;  
16. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning Formation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 4578);  
17. Regional Regulation of Maluku Province Number 02 of 2012 concerning Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence in Maluku;  
18. Decree of the Governor of Maluku Number 302 of 2007 concerning Establishment of Integrated Service Center for Women and Children (P2TPA);  
19. Regional Regulation of Tual City Number 02 of 2016 concerning Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus of Tual City (Regional Gazette of Tual City of 2016 Number 88, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Tual City Number 7096);  

With Mutual Approval

# REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF TUAL CITY

# MAYOR OF TUAL

